!/tests/**
/tests/**/__pycache__/
/tests/**/*.py[cod]

# The test_*.py rule above targets throwaway probe scripts dropped in the repo
# root. It must never hide the real suite: without this negation any NEW file
# under tests/ is silently untracked and CI runs green against nothing.
# Scoped deliberately to tests/ only - a broader negation would re-expose the
# *.db / *.env rules above and leak real user transcripts and API keys.
!tests/**/*.py
!tests/**/*.js
!tests/**/*.json


